<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ferry and trawler collide at Cork.</title>
<headline>Ferry and trawler collide at Cork.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A car ferry and a small trawler were involved in a minor collision as they entered Cork harbour early Monday, Cork Port authorities said.</p>
<p>The incident involved &quot;The Superferry&quot; operated by Swansea Cork Ferries and the 55ft &quot;Jonara&quot;. It happened at about 0625 at Roches Point at the harbour entrance.</p>
<p>The car ferry was undamaged but some damage was caused to the fishing vessel, which also took on some water a port official said. An inquiry is under way.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom + 353 1 676 9775</p>
